{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "It's that important, huh?": "",
  "Just let it go, man. I'm not joking about killing you.": "",
  "(I've gotta say, the lengths he's going to make sure we don't see that bag are pretty suspicious.)": "",
  "(White pants. That's the same color Ono Michio wears.)": "",
  "Hey, what are you looking at?": "",
  "(That won't be enough proof...)": "",
  "You don't carry a bag?": "",
  "So the bag in the hallway isn't yours?": "",
  "(He really doesn't know about the bag? Or is he playing dumb?)": "",
  "White pants. The same color as the robber.": "",
  "(I can't rule out the possibility, despite whatever faith Hironaka-san seems to have in him.)": "",
  "Mind if I take a quick look in your bag?": "",
  "(Just a wallet and some plushie he probably won in a claw machine.)": "",
  "(It has to be somewhere in this arcade... But where?)": "",
  "Hey, did you see anything? Anything that might help?": "",
  "Huh? Nah. I was dozing off in the back.": "",
  "(Useless.)": "",
  "Oh, a security camera! I should have thought of that earlier!": "",
  "Don't bother. The staff already told me it's a fake.": "",
  "Well, that's a shame. We'd have solved this in seconds, otherwise.": "",
  "What's back here?": "",
  "A one-stall bathroom. I looked, but everything seemed fine.": "",
  "A trash can for recycling. And inside we have...": "",
  "Empty cans. Yep.": "",
  "Huh? How?": "",
  "I guess those boots would be hard to run in. But if the anti-theft paint ball was used...": "",
  "Then they may still be wearing sneakers stained with that paint.": "",
  "I guess they would have just discarded the boots, too.": "",
  "(I think I've gotten what I can out of the costume.)": "",
  "(There's probably nothing else I'm going to find.)": "",
  "You're wearing sandals. Kind of uncommon in the winter, wouldn't you say?": "",
  "Yeah, but I live pretty close by, and putting on shoes sucks.": "",
  "Yeah, I know that feeling.": "",
  "(He's not wearing sneakers and there's no anti-theft paint on him. Pretty clean, so far.)": "",
  "(These aren't boots, and there's not a spot of anti-theft paint on them. Probably not it.)": "",
  "(If he's the culprit, that would mean he changed his shoes.)": "",
  "Wait, are those boots?": "",
  "Yeah, but Ono Michio wears <font_kind=yakuza_italic>cool</font_kind> boots that are vital for any fisherman.": "",
  "Oh. So your boots aren't cool, I guess.": "",
  "(He's not wearing sneakers, and I don't see any paint. Hm.)": "",
  "(Sandals with ankle length pants... Wouldn't that be pretty cold?)": "",
  "What are you looking at?": "",
  "I was just wondering why you'd wear sandals in this weather, especially with pants like that.": "",
  "Wait, sandals?": "",
  "Oh, crap...": "",
  "Huh? Oh, just thought of something, that's all. It's nothing.": "",
  "(Why do I get the feeling he didn't even realize he was wearing sandals?)": "",
  "Yagami-san, wasn't that kind of suspicious?": "",
  "Yeah, I should probably take a closer look at those sandals.": "",
  "Huh? It is?": "",
  "Yeah, I'm not so sure anymore. But I made it sound good, right?": "",
  "Yagami-san! Do you even know what you're talking about!?": "",
  "Y-Yes! My hand just slipped, okay!?": "",
  "I have?": "",
  "Oh yeah! Duh!": "",
  "Hey! Start talking! Where's my money!?": "",
  "Are you done investigating, Yagami-san?": "",
  "You do!? Who is it!?": "",
  "(I better investigate the scene a little more.)": "",
  "(Wait, there's something written on the heel.)": "",
  "When and how did he pay back his debts?": "",
  "That explains everything.": "",
  "(Suspicious sandals... Hmmm.)": "",
  "(I can't leave them hanging like this... I need to accuse a culprit.)": "",
  "Nobody here seems to have noticed it happen.": "",
  "I think I've got a good inventory of the robber's belongings now...": "",
  "But it's odd... Something's missing.": "",
  "And I have a pretty good idea who the culprit is.": "",
  "Pardon me, sir, but could you spare a moment of your time? My name is Sagara, and I'm the manager of this establishment.": "",
  "We're currently hosting the Battle of the Alps, our special coffee cupping event.": "",
  "You can try out several kinds of coffee for free, so there's no loss to your wallet. Sounds like a fair challenge, yes?": "",
  "Free coffee...": "",
  "Mm, I'll pass for now.": "",
  "Very well then, sir.": "",
  "You're welcome to try it out whenever you wish. Please come back and visit us again!": "",
  "I'm up for a challenge. How's this whole cupping thing work?": "",
  "Well then, allow me to explain the process.": "",
  "I will begin by describing four types of our finest coffees.": "",
  "Afterward, you will select one cup of coffee to drink with your eyes closed...": "",
  "Then, I will ask you to guess which coffee that was. Simple enough, yes?": "",
  "Sounds good to me. I'm Yagami, by the way.": "",
  "Well then, Yagami-sama! Are you ready to battle the Alps?": "",
  "I've <font_kind=yakuza_italic>bean</font_kind> ready. Hehe.": "",
  "Yeah, I can imagine what that would taste like.": "",
  "Splendid.": "",
  "Before we begin, I'd like to give you some tips on proper coffee cupping.": "",
  "The easiest flavors to recognize in a coffee are bitterness and sourness.": "",
  "People might describe these flavors as sharp or even pungent.": "",
  "Now, the tricky flavor here is richness. This can be a pretty vague sensation.": "",
  "In our café, we define richness as the following:": "",
  "A deep, full-bodied flavor that lingers in your mouth for a long while.": "",
  "In other words, it certainly isn't light... and lacks any sort of bite to it.": "",
  "Mm. Taste is quite a complex sensation, wouldn't you say?": "",
  "It encompasses more than just what sits on the tongue. For example, how something smells or feels...": "",
  "Some may say taste is all subjective, but I'm convinced that's the very reason we can enjoy it. Because it is so broad.": "",
  "Does that not seem to be the case?": "",
  "Quite so. Now without further ado, I will share with you our coffees of the day.": "",
  "For your tasting pleasure, we're offering <t:select_random=1>, <t:select_random=2>, <t:select_random=3>, and <t:select_random=4>.": "",
  "Blue Mountain, esteemed as \"The King of Coffee Beans,\" is one of our most popular coffees, and a standard of our menu.": "",
  "It boasts a refined scent, smooth texture, and a tripartite balance of bitterness, and richness, and sourness.": "",
  "Jamaican coffee is known worldwide for its dark, bitter flavor that also boasts a wonderful splash of sweetness...": "",
  "Mocha is distinct for its rich, bitter flavor that lingers on the tongue. It also bears a bold, fruity sourness.": "",
  "True. I'm not quite sure what you mean by that.": "",
  "Blended coffee is what we're famous for at Café Alps. We generally serve this fine roast as part of our breakfast set...": "",
  "Okay. I think I'm starting to get it.": "",
  "You make a valid point. There really is a lot that goes into breaking down the meaning of flavor, isn't there?": "",
  "Kona is a famous type of coffee that hails from Hawaii. It's known for its strong, refreshing sourness...": "",
  "Wow, you actually memorized all that? That's nuts...": "",
  "(I see. So I should look at the chart and take a good note of the taste.)": "",
  "(It's very acidic, that's for sure. Also bitter, but rich and velvety as well. The flavor really lingers on the tongue.)": "",
  "(Ooh, this coffee's <font_kind=yakuza_italic>got 'em all in</font_kind> here! It's bitter, acidic, and even kind of fruity. Yet they all harmonize together.)": "",
  "Toraja coffee boasts a powerful bitter flavor and an unparalleled, full-bodied taste.": "",
  "In addition, it barely contains a hint of sourness.": "",
  "Guatemalan coffee features a fruity, sour flavor which is balanced well by its bitterness...": "",
  "Java Robusta is low on sourness and is recognized for its rich scent, similar to burnt wheat.": "",
  "Ahaha. What can I say, I simply adore coffee's intricate delicacies. Now, please remain waiting in your seat.": "",
  "I'll be out shortly with the coffee, so please have a seat.": "",
  "Now, go on. You can only taste one sip of the coffee.": "",
  "So, have you decided on your answer?": "",
  "Is that your final answer? Very well, then...": "",
  "Unfortunately, your choice was incorrect.": "",
  "The one you drank was Blue Mountain.": "",
  "The one you drank was Jamaican.": "",
  "The one you drank was Mocha.": "",
  "I believe that people are drawn to its rich, bitter taste that pairs well with chocolate or even steamed milk.": "",
  "(...Now, which coffee is this?)": "",
  "The one you drank was Blended Coffee.": "",
  "Yeah. I'm pretty sure it was this one.": "",
  "The one you drank was Kona.": "",
  "Man, I used to think once you tried one coffee, you tried them all. Guess I'd better train my taste buds.": "",
  "The one you drank was Toraja.": "",
  "Yeah, it felt like I could concentrate more on each distinct aspect by keeping my eyes closed.": "",
  "The one you drank was Guatemalan.": "",
  "The one you drank was Java Robusta.": "",
  "Quite so. Now, were you able to fully savor the decadent and intricate facets of coffee drinking due to keeping your eyes closed?": "",
  "Is there a particular reason why you went with a blind taste test?": "",
  "Splendid! Then I'd say this coffee cupping event I've planned has certainly done its job.": "",
  "That... is possibly the most inspiring coffee speech I've ever heard. And I'd honestly have to agree. Today was fun.": "",
  "Well, as I've hopefully demonstrated to you, I consider myself a coffee aficionado... I cherish it with all my heart.": "",
  "But I feel as though a lot of people these days have a hard time choosing what to drink.": "",
  "Sure. I'll stop by next time I need a caffeine boost.": "",
  "While I do pride myself on knowing coffee's many subtleties, in the end it all comes down to individual preference.": "",
  "I'm assuming that's a good thing.": "",
  "Oh! Pardon me, sir, may I have a little bit of your time?": "",
  "Sure, what's going on?": "",
  "Unfortunately, I seem to have caught a cold, and one of our guests is requesting Blue Mountain coffee.": "",
  "That doesn't sound good. But hey, I'm sure you of all people can tell the difference just by smell and taste alone.": "",
  "Now, normally this wouldn't be an issue...": "",
  "But the label on the container peeled off and I can't tell which bean is which!": "",
  "Ah, okay. So that's what's going on. ": "",
  "Well, you see... I can't smell or taste much of anything because of this awful cold...": "",
  "Yeah. I can see why you wouldn't want to piss him off...": "",
  "To make matters worse, this customer is quite... <font_kind=yakuza_italic>particular</font_kind> about his coffee. He says he won't drink anything but Blue Mountain.": "",
  "And I refuse... *sniff* ...to serve... *sniffle* ...the wrong one! Ah-Achoo!!! ": "",
  "Indeed. As such, I have a favor I'd like to ask.": "",
  "You want <font_kind=yakuza_italic>me</font_kind>? Wouldn't your coworkers be more suited for this?": "",
  "Could you please taste our coffee to find out which one is Blue Mountain?": "",
  "We do, but they all seem to be lacking in confidence... and courage.": "",
  "Exactly. Worst-case scenario, he might even demand my pinky!": "",
  "I see... Well, he does seem like the type who'd take a couple swings at you if you served him the wrong cup.": "",
  "So, how about it? Will you help me out? We coffee connoisseurs need to stick together, you know!": "",
  "Th-Thank y... y... yaaa-chooo!!! *sniffle* Thank you!": "",
  "Ahah... I doubt he'd go that far...": "",
  "Hmm... In that case, I'll see what I can do.": "",
  "I can try. Let's start with this one.": "",
  "Here is what I'd like you to try...": "",
  "(So this one's got a nice, rich texture and a fruity, acidic flavor. And it's bitter. Huh, there's a lot going on here.)": "",
  "(Bitter. Acidic. Rich. All well-balanced and indistinct from one another...)": "",
  "(It's light, with a very pleasant aroma. The kind that'd make you climb a mountain for just a single sip.)": "",
  "It must be either of these. Can you tell which is Blue Mountain?": "",
  "(...But still, this is pretty hard.)": "",
  "Yeah, I think it's the first one.": "",
  "Ready to move on to the next one?": "",
  "(Hope I got it right...)": "",
  "Well? Did you discover the Blue Mountain?": "",
  "Yeah, I think it's the second one.": "",
  "Sorry, can I take another sip?": "",
  "Are you certain?": "",
  "Shoot! I messed up!": "",
  "Damn! I have to do something, fast!": "",
  "I understand. Then I'll trust your judgment and serve this to our guest.": "",
  "Hey, it's only coffee, man. There's no need to threaten someone's pinky over it.": "",
  "No need. This never would've happened if I chose the right cup.": "",
  "(Why... Why is he crying!?)": "",
  "Wha...?": "",
  "I'm terribly sorry, sir!　": "",
  "(That was pretty random, but I'm glad I got it right!)": "",
  "Eek!! I knew it!": "",
  "Please let us make up for serving the wrong coffee, sir. We won't charge you anything.": "",
  "Thank you for your help, Yagami-sama.": "",
  "Yeah! I guess I did!": "",
  "The fault does not lie with you. After all, you only recently began your coffee tasting journey.": "",
  "Wow, a special coffee? Just for me?": "",
  "And besides, my pinky remains fully intact. So I really can't complain.": "",
  "S-Sir, is there a problem? Does it taste less than... spectacular?": "",
  "Good show, Yagami-sama! You did it!": "",
  "World's rarest, you say?": "",
  "M-My pleasure! Thank you for coming in today, sir!": "",
  "10,000 yen for just one cup!? Get outta here!": "",
  "Yagami-san, I know it's not much... But I've prepared you a special coffee as a way of saying thanks.": "",
  "Kopi Luwak, huh...": "",
  "Yes, it's considered one of the world's rarest coffees.": "",
  "Yes. It's an exquisite, expensive bean that can only be procured by established coffee traders.": "",
  "What...? So you're telling me it's watered-down cat poop!?": "",
  "Sometimes it can cost over 30,000 yen per 100 grams, and a single cup can be sold for as much as 10,000 yen.": "",
  "People should simply choose what they like, as long as the drink tastes good to them. I firmly believe that.": "",
  "That is why I put together a special event...": "",
  "Where people can enjoy their coffee, worry-free!": "",
  "Why thank you! I'll be here anytime, so please feel free to challenge your perception of taste and try our coffee again!": "",
  "I hope with today's tasting, you've come to appreciate all that coffee has to offer. Please try our challenge again!": "",
  "The coffee you chose... is...": "",
  "Correct! You, sir, have the palate of a veritable epicurean! Cheers to you!": "",
  "Thanks. I guess my palate's getting better every time, huh?": "",
  "Indeed! After all, the true measure of a man is decided not by how many coffees he drinks, but how well he enjoys them.": "",
  "Haha, I feel you. Then I'll be sure to drop by again.": "",
  "Correct! Congratulations, you got it right again! I must admit, I'm quite impressed.": "",
  "Thanks. I think I'm slowly starting to understand just how complex the world of coffee can be.": "",
  "I'm elated to hear that, Yagami-sama. Please come back as often as you'd like!": "",
  "Most definitely. See you around.": "",
  "(Coffee really does taste different depending on the bean.)": "",
  "(Maybe I should brew nicer coffee in the office sometime?)": "",
  "This... This flavor...": "",
  "This ain't Blue Mountain at all! This is Guatemalaaaaan!!!": "",
  "...You fuckin' with me? Huh!? Tell me why a place called \"Café Alps\" can't at least pour the right coffee!": "",
  "Now I wouldn't be a yakuza if I let you off the hook with just an apology, so I'll chop yer pinky like a baby carrot!": "",
  "Sorry... I just get so worked up. I can never keep calm when it comes to my daily cup of joe.": "",
  "You won't? Well hot damn. I'll take it!": "",
  "This... This coffee...": "",
  "Ooh... *sob*": "",
  "No, in fact... it tastes just like home.": "",
  "My Ma, she... she loves coffee.": "",
  "She would often buy us Blue Mountain the day after my Pa's check came in.": "",
  "This cup... it tastes exactly like the ones I used to have... back when times were good.": "",
  "Thanks for the caffeine-induced trip down memory lane. This is the best I've had in a long, long time.": "",
  "That is correct. The name of this fabled bean is... Kopi Luwak.": "",
  "It's made from beans that are harvested from the feces of the Asian palm civet, or <font_kind=yakuza_italic>luwak</font_kind>. It looks much like a kitten.": "",
  "Oh, come now. The palm civet is an exotic animal that eats ripe coffee beans as part of its regular diet.": "",
  "These scrumptious, naturally selected coffee beans are then fermented in its digestive tract and later expelled.": "",
  "Wow. I can only imagine what the aftertaste is like.": "",
  "Don't forget to finish it before it gets cold, Yagami-san. Drink up!": "",
  "Can't believe I'm about to sip this up... Well, here goes nothing.": "",
  "Whoa, this is... actually really delicious.": "",
  "It is, isn't it!?": "",
  "But 10,000 yen per cup? It's definitely not something I can drink on the regular.": "",
  "Certainly. But if it does please your taste buds, we'll always have it stocked just for you, Yagami-sama.": "",
  "After all, you're our most valued customer.": "",
  "No kidding? Thanks, that means a lot.": "",
  "Of course. We look forward to your next visit, sir.": "",
  "The base fare is 410 yen. Where would you like to go?": "",
  "Very well. I hope to see you again soon.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "What are you looking at?": "มองอะไรอยู่",
  "Wha...?": "อะ...ไร...?",
  "The base fare is 410 yen. Where would you like to go?": "ค่าโดยสารเริ่มต้นอยู่ที่ 410 เยนครับ จะไปที่ไหนดีครับ?",
  "Very well. I hope to see you again soon.": "ได้เลยครับ หวังว่าจะได้พบกันอีกเร็วๆนี้นะครับ"
 }
}
